; Two diodes and a source, with the circuit's variational equations: a
; source s drives an inductor and a diode in series into a node held by a
; capacitor, a second diode and a conductance g to ground. In the diodes'
; own units - currents in units of the first diode's saturation current,
; voltages in units of the thermal voltage, time in units that make the
; inductance and the capacitance one - Shockley's law gives the series
; diode's voltage at its current j as log1p(j), and the shunt diode's
; current at its voltage v as k expm1(v), k its saturation current in the
; first's units: the math library's log1p and expm1, each a routine inlined
; (M1's build, item 4), with its rule in the tangent, select(r == r,
; da / (1 + a), r) and (1 + r) * da. log1p's domain is the diode's: no
; current below -1, the saturation current, flows backward through it.
system diode
format fp256
round  rne
state  j, v
tangent w
param  s = 6, k = 1/8, g = 1/4
d/dt j = s - log1p(j) - v
d/dt v = j - k * expm1(v) - g * v
step   rk4, h = 1/64
